    "details_md": "{\n  \"summary\": \"Write a comprehensive human-facing docs/ set on how slopwork works, accurate to the shipped CLI/code (verified, not aspirational). Cover: overview/getting-started, concepts (ticket/edge/session/event/actor model, the state machine, derived blocked/stale/ready overlays, the flatfile JSONC db + git-merge story), full CLI command reference (every command, flags, exit codes, examples), the agent workflow loop + house rules, the read-only web UI, configuration (config.yaml, env vars, actor/harness resolution, transcripts modes), and the concurrency/lock-free-updates/sandbox model. Link the set from README.\",\n  \"acceptance\": [\"docs/ contains an indexed, comprehensive set (getting-started, concepts, cli-reference, agent-workflow, web-ui, configuration, concurrency+merging)\", \"every command/flag/exit-code claim cross-checked against ./dist/slop --help and the code\", \"README links to docs/; no inaccuracies\", \"docs use the name slopwork and the binary slop consistently\"],\n  \"context\": [\"./dist/slop --help + each command --help\", \"design.md (source of truth to distill for users)\", \"src/cli/commands/*, src/core/entities/*\", \"README.md (link target)\"]\n}",
